--TEST--
a `|>` whose right side never names `$_` is refused, because the left side has nowhere to go — `rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once`'s E0129
--FILE--
<?nvs
// rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once — the hole appears exactly once on a
// right side, so a right side carrying none is a refusal and not a discarded
// left side.
string $padded = "  x  ";
echo $padded |> Core\Str::trim("y"), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0129]: the right side of `|>` needs the hole `$_`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
